{
	"title": "Est-ce un multiple ?",
	"description": "Dire si un entier jusqu'à 999 est un multiple de 3, 4, 6, 7, 8 ou 9 (141 n'est pas multiple de 7) ; trouver le multiple parmi quatre nombres",
	"grades": ["CM1"],
	"theme": "Entiers",
	"domain": "Diviser",
	"subdomain": "Multiples et diviseurs",
	"level": 2,
	"delay": 30,
	"status": "draft",
	"options": {
		"constraints": {
			"spacesFromFourDigits": true
		}
	},
	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "Le nombre ${{n}}$ est-il un multiple de ${{d}}$ ?\n\n```choix\nmelanger: non\n- Oui\n- Non\n```",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "d",
					"expression": "3|4|6|7|8|9"
				},
				{
					"name": "o",
					"expression": "0..1"
				},
				{
					"name": "q",
					"expression": "4..140"
				},
				{
					"name": "dm",
					"expression": "eval:d-1"
				},
				{
					"name": "s",
					"expression": "1..{{dm}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "r",
					"expression": "eval:s*o"
				},
				{
					"name": "n",
					"expression": "eval:d*q+r"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["n>=20", "n<=999"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{o}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"**Multiple.** ${{n}}$ est un multiple de ${{d}}$ si la division de ${{n}}$ par ${{d}}$ tombe juste : le reste est $0$.",
					"$${{n}} = {{d}} \\times {{q}}{{if:o==1| + {{r}}|}}$$",
					"{{if:o==0|Le reste est $0$ : \\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{oui}, ${{n}}$ est un multiple de ${{d}}$ (il est dans la table de ${{d}}$).|Le reste est ${{r}}$, pas $0$ : \\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{non}, ${{n}}$ n'est pas un multiple de ${{d}}$.}}"
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "Lequel de ces nombres est un multiple de ${{d}}$ ?\n\n```choix\n- ${{m0}}$\n- ${{m1}}$\n- ${{m2}}$\n- ${{m3}}$\n```",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "d",
					"expression": "3|4|6|7|8|9"
				},
				{
					"name": "dm",
					"expression": "eval:d-1"
				},
				{
					"name": "q0",
					"expression": "10..110"
				},
				{
					"name": "q1",
					"expression": "10..110"
				},
				{
					"name": "q2",
					"expression": "10..110"
				},
				{
					"name": "q3",
					"expression": "10..110"
				},
				{
					"name": "r1",
					"expression": "1..{{dm}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "r2",
					"expression": "1..{{dm}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "r3",
					"expression": "1..{{dm}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "m0",
					"expression": "eval:d*q0"
				},
				{
					"name": "m1",
					"expression": "eval:d*q1+r1"
				},
				{
					"name": "m2",
					"expression": "eval:d*q2+r2"
				},
				{
					"name": "m3",
					"expression": "eval:d*q3+r3"
				}
			],
			"conditions": [
				"m0<=999",
				"m1<=999",
				"m2<=999",
				"m3<=999",
				"q1!=q2",
				"q1!=q3",
				"q2!=q3",
				"q0!=q1",
				"q0!=q2",
				"q0!=q3"
			],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "0"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"**Multiple.** Un multiple de ${{d}}$ est un nombre de la table de ${{d}}$ : sa division par ${{d}}$ tombe juste.",
					"$${{m0}} = {{d}} \\times {{q0}}$$ Le reste est $0$ : $\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{m0}}}$ est un multiple de ${{d}}$.",
					"Les autres ne le sont pas : ${{m1}} = {{d}} \\times {{q1}} + {{r1}}$, ${{m2}} = {{d}} \\times {{q2}} + {{r2}}$, ${{m3}} = {{d}} \\times {{q3}} + {{r3}}$."
				]
			}
		}
	],
